# U-Boot-proper's pre-relocation reserve region. zynq-common.h pins that region
# to an 8 KiB window in high OCM (CFG_SYS_INIT_RAM_ADDR 0xFFFF0000 + SIZE 0x2000),
# so gd + malloc_f + stack for the bigger FDT grow past 0xFFFF0000 into unmapped
# space -> data abort (DFAR 0xfffefe38). Move U-Boot-proper's pre-reloc stack
# into DRAM (already brought up by the SPL) so the reserve chain has room; the
# SPL keeps its own OCM stack (CONFIG_SPL_STACK, SPL_SHARES_INIT_SP_ADDR unset).
# 0x03f00000 sits in DRAM just below the u-boot text base (0x04000000), clear of
# the SPL BSS/stack (0x100000/0x200000) and the top-of-DRAM relocation target.
