# USB-gadget re-imaging over the OTG port (no card pull needed):
#   ums 0 mmc 0:1      -> export the ESP (FAT) to the host as mass storage.
#                         USE THE :1 FORM. The bare `ums 0 mmc 0` is the
#                         whole-disk form: cmd/usb_mass_storage.c maps partnum
#                         0 to sector 0..lba, so it offers the partition
#                         table, the ESP *and* the rootfs to the host
#                         read-write with no confirmation. A host that
#                         automounts and replays a log has then written to the
#                         board's rootfs. :1 limits the blast radius to the
#                         ESP, which is the partition re-imaging actually
#                         needs (uboot.env, boot.scr, the bitstream).
